### Weather Image App - API documentation
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or JetBrains HTTP client).
### Replace @host with your deployed Function App host, then run the requests
### top-to-bottom: start a job, copy the returned jobId, then poll the status.

# ---- Choose an environment -------------------------------------------------
# Local (func start):
# @host = http://localhost:7071

# Deployed Function App (live):
@host = https://weatherimg-z7idlr2ityrks.azurewebsites.net

@baseUrl = {{host}}/api

### 1. Start a new image-creation job.
# Returns 202 Accepted with a unique jobId and a status URL.
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

###

# Capture the jobId from the response above and paste it here:
@jobId = REPLACE-WITH-RETURNED-JOBID

### 2. Fetch job status + generated image links.
# While running: status "Running", completed < total.
# When finished: status "Completed", "images" holds one SAS link per station.
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}

###
